Z||000009||theogre||12-02-2001||01:11 PM||||It's not rocket science but you wouldn't want to pay to have it done. I can't imagine a qualified shop charging less than a grand to do it. And that's just labor. When I worked in a shop, I wouldn't have done it for much less than that. It's allot of time. Even then you can't gurantee no problems. look how many people here have clutch problems on cars that came with stick.<P>The ECM PROM needs to be changed at the very least.<P>You need to fabricate a new hydraulic line. Not even worth messing with the old one beyond using it for a pattern.<P>you need to fart around under the dash and figure out what to do with the neutral saftey interlock. Also need to remove the ignition park interlock.<P>You need to change the whole shifter set and cables. Hopefully all the parts are good and nothing breaks trying to get it from one car to another.<P>Then you have all the normal BS with changing the tranny and installing a clutch. You've also got to make sure the tranny doesn't need any seals or clutch arm parts.||||reg||1
